    "sixtySeconds": {
      "whatItDoes": "Spleeter is Deezer's source separation library, written in Python on TensorFlow. Its pretrained models split music into 2 stems (vocals and accompaniment), 4 stems (vocals, drums, bass, other) or 5 stems (adding piano). You can use it from the command line or as a Python library, and you can train your own models if you have isolated-source data.",
      "problem": "Getting a clean vocal or instrumental track from a finished song is hard without the original multitrack. Spleeter does it quickly with pretrained models.",
